<article class="env-lemma" id="005I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/005I">Lemma <span data-tag="005I">5.15.3</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a continuous map of topological spaces. If the inverse image of every retrocompact open subset of $Y$ is retrocompact in $X$, then inverse images of constructible sets are constructible. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $f^{-1}(U \cap V^ c) = f^{-1}(U) \cap f^{-1}(V)^ c$, combined with the definition of constructible sets. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>